// Goods: bulk quantities held in settlement stockpiles (milestone 2).
// unit: what one unit of the good is. Food goods are counted in person-years: one unit feeds
// one person for a year.
// spoilage: share of a stock lost per year in store.
// weight: how heavy one unit is to carry, relative to a person-year of grain (used by trade).
// tier: the need it meets: life, everyday, luxury, or none for materials.
// food: true if people can eat it.
// Goods made from others come after their inputs (recipes.json), so what a settlement wants of
// a material can be worked out from what it wants of the goods made from it.
// value: the good's base price in food (person-years of grain); local prices rise above it
// where the good is scarce and fall below it where it is plentiful (prices.json).
